<footer class="[&_*]:transition-colors [&_*]:text-muted/50 [&:hover_*]:text-muted/80 [&_a:hover]:text-muted [&_.footer-extras]:transition-opacity [&_.footer-extras]:invisible [&:hover_.footer-extras]:visible py-2 mt-10">
  <p class="text-center">
    <%= help_message if current_user && local_assigns[:help_message] != false %>
  </p>
  <p class="text-xs text-center">
    <%# AGPL-3.0 + CLAUDE.md Rule 7: this attribution is required. "HCB" here names
        the upstream project, not Fuime — do not rebrand it. %>
    Fuime is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/hackclub/hcb" target="_blank" class="underline">HCB</a> by Hack Club (AGPL-3.0).
  </p>

  <%# Fuime: legal links live here, not in .footer-extras below — that block is
      `invisible` until the footer is hovered, which is not a reachable place to
      put the terms someone is being asked to agree to. %>
  <p class="text-xs text-center flex justify-center gap-1 flex-wrap">
    <%= link_to "Terms", terms_path %>
    •
    <%= link_to "Privacy", privacy_path %>
    •
    <%= link_to "Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path %>
    •
    <%= link_to "FAQ", faq_path %>
  </p>

  <%# Standing status disclosure. Fuime shows balances, ledgers and cards, which is
      exactly the presentation that invites a reader to assume a bank and deposit
      insurance sit behind it. 12 CFR 328.102(b)(3)(ii) treats omitting the
      information needed to prevent that assumption as the violation, so this is
      stated unconditionally rather than only on money-related pages, and it is in
      the always-visible block for the same reason the legal links are.
      When a partner bank exists, this becomes the "banking services provided by
      [Bank], Member FDIC" form — until then, naming a bank here would itself be
      the false claim. %>
  <%# The entity is named here and not only in the terms because this is the
      disclosure a reader sees without clicking anything, and "Fuime is a
      financial technology company" invited the reading that Fuime IS the
      company. It is a product; the company is the one that would answer for it. %>
  <p class="text-xs text-center mx-auto" style="max-width: 44rem;">
    Fuime is a product of <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>,
    a financial technology company, not a bank. Fuime does not hold
    deposits and does not offer FDIC-insured products. Payments are processed by
    Stripe. Venture accounts are opened and owned by a parent or legal guardian;
    young founders operate them with guardian oversight.
  </p>

  <% if !Rails.env.production? || auditor_signed_in? %>
    <% @sql_cached_count = ActiveRecord::RuntimeRegistry.stats.cached_queries_count %>
    <% @sql_count = ActiveRecord::RuntimeRegistry.stats.queries_count - @sql_cached_count %>
    <p class="text-center text-xs">
      Loaded using <%= @sql_count %> unique
      SQL <%= "query".pluralize @sql_count %> (+ <%= @sql_cached_count %>
      cached). Running on Rails <%= Rails::VERSION::STRING %> with
      Ruby <%= RUBY_VERSION %>.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <p class="footer-extras text-xs flex justify-center gap-1">
    <% if Build.commit_hash.present? %>
      <% build_info = capture do %>
        <span class="tooltipped tooltipped--n tooltipped--xl underline" aria-label="Build <%= Build.commit_name %>">
          <%= Build.age.present? ? "Last built #{Build.age} ago" : "Build info" %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
      <%# Only link to GitHub if the build is not dirty. Otherwise, just show build info with no link. %>
      <%= link_to_if !Build.commit_dirty?, build_info, "#{Rails.configuration.constants.github_url}/commit/#{Build.commit_hash}", target: "_blank" %>
      •
    <% end %>
    <%= link_to "Security", security_path %>
    •
    <%= link_to "API docs", docs_api_index_path %>
    •
    <%= link_to "Open source", Rails.configuration.constants.github_url %>
  </p>
</footer>
